@ProductCatalog.API_HostAddress = http://localhost:5088

@host = http://localhost:5088
@productId = 1
@secondProductId = 2

### Create new product first (copy returned id and set @productId)
POST {{host}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "SKU-1",
  "name": "Product",
  "price": 199.99
}

###

### Create duplicate SKU (expected 409 Conflict)
POST {{host}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "SKU-1",
  "name": "Product Duplicate",
  "price": 199.99
}

###

### First read after product exists (expected cache miss + set)
GET {{host}}/api/products/{{productId}}
Accept: application/json

###

### Second read (expected cache hit)
GET {{host}}/api/products/{{productId}}
Accept: application/json

###

### Update existing product
PUT {{host}}/api/products/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Product Updated",
  "price": 149.50
}

###

### Read after update (should return latest value)
GET {{host}}/api/products/{{productId}}
Accept: application/json

###

### Create second product after updating product 1
# @name createSecondProduct
POST {{host}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "SKU-2",
  "name": "Product",
  "price": 249.99
}

### Set @secondProductId from the POST response id when needed

### Read second product
GET {{host}}/api/products/{{secondProductId}}
Accept: application/json

###

### Not found scenario
GET {{host}}/api/products/999999
Accept: application/json

###

### Validation scenario (bad request)
POST {{host}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "",
  "name": "",
  "price": -10
}
 